  "updateinfo_id": "ALSA-2026:82807",
  "description": "The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * kernel: openvswitch: defer tunnel netdev_put to RCU release (CVE-2026-31678)\n  * kernel: ipv6: validate extension header length before copying to cmsg (CVE-2026-63920)\n  * kernel: drm/amd/display: set new_stream to NULL after release (CVE-2026-68236)\n  * kernel: drm/dp/mst: fix buffer overflows in sideband chunk accumulation (CVE-2026-68278)\n  * kernel: wifi: mac80211: defer link RX stats percpu free to RCU (CVE-2026-68409)\n  * kernel: drm/amdgpu/vce: fix integer overflow in image size (CVE-2026-68108)\n  * kernel: cifs: validate DFS referral string offsets (CVE-2026-72318)\n  * kernel: drm/vmwgfx: use check_add_overflow for shader size+offset bound (CVE-2026-80887)\n  * kernel: drm/amdkfd: Add TLB flush after MES queue eviction/suspension (CVE-2026-89811)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
  "fromstr": "packager@almalinux.org",
